findings.description:
The arch's NFR for the tick path is "tens of thousands of agents at full behavioral fidelity on a single CPU process". The slice touches that hot path but only says it targets "the hundreds-of-agents scale" (line 173). It never restates the arch target or sets a tick-time budget at a reference agent count.

The brute-force query can legitimately fall short of the arch target until (105). But the slice should:
- restate the arch NFR;
- state that (100) is not expected to meet it;
- name what it does guarantee. One option is a measured tick time at N=1,000 as a baseline for (105) to compare against.
